        <headline>Special Weather Statement issued September 24 at 4:07PM MST by NWS Phoenix AZ</headline>
        <description>At 407 PM MST, Doppler radar was tracking a cluster of strong
thunderstorms extending from 6 miles north of Superior to 6 miles
south of Superior, moving west at 15 mph.

HAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and pea size hail.

SOURCE...Radar indicated.

IMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around
unsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is
possible.

Locations impacted include...
Superior, Boyce Thompson Arboretum and Queen Valley.
</description>
        <instruction>Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening
weather conditions.</instruction>
